Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Add gromen-inflate scene: "The Only Exit / Inflating the
 debt away"
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A third-person, AI-narrated summary of Luke Gromen's FFTT video "Does the
Administration believe they can inflate US debt to sustainability?"
(recorded Oct 7 2026). Copied from gromen-certainty and adapted.

Diagram (src/main.rs): one world of four regions the camera pans between,
keyed to the ten cue ids intro, measure, covid, proof, ai, others, japan,
dollar, loop, gold:
  A  true interest expense (interest, entitlements, veterans) against tax
     receipts; 2020 at 110% with the Fed printing the gap; rates 0%,
     inflation ~10%, Debt/GDP counting 130% -> 115% in 18 months
  B  four exits as doors; 2, 3, 4 are considered and crossed out, and the
     film ends here with door 1 lit, "short bonds" struck, gold/silver/a
     little bitcoin rising
  C  Japan vs USA
  D  the strong-dollar option rejected, and the doom loop accelerating
The lower-left beat labels are each block's caption text (one shortened).
The on-screen credit reads "AI-NARRATED SUMMARY · source: Luke Gromen,
FFTT, Oct 7 2026"; nothing is labelled dramatized or first person.

voice.py: mastering keeps the lines without a `lead` (intro..japan) level
and rises only over the pushed lines (dollar, loop, gold). MAX_TOKENS
raised, since the seven-line calm take runs ~47 s.

build.sh: --publish takes --private (default), --public or --tunnel and
passes it to the deploy script as its first argument; publish dir is
$REPORTS_DIR/gromen-inflate-YYYYMMDD.

package.py: new title and an honest description linking the original
video; the upstream revision in reproduce.sh comes from git merge-base.

Known narration defect: the calm take (take 0) is too long for Orpheus.
Seeds 1 and 2 dropped the last sentence (unusable); seed 3, committed
here, is complete except that the `proof` line skips the words "Debt to
GDP fell from 130% to 115%" (the caption and diagram still show them).
Three seeds is the limit, so the take needs splitting in script.json.

