+# The Only Exit / Inflating the debt away
+
+One Scene Plan, one diagram, no cuts. A third-person, AI-narrated summary, in
+our own words, of Luke Gromen's FFTT video "Does the Administration believe they
+can inflate US debt to sustainability?" (recorded Oct 7 2026,
+https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=INgvg03agP8). It is not his voice, not a
+recording, and not endorsed by him; the film carries "AI-NARRATED SUMMARY ·
+source: Luke Gromen, FFTT, Oct 7 2026" on screen throughout and the page says so too.
+
+## Change the script, rebuild, ship
+
+1. Edit `narration/script.json`. Each entry in `clips[0].blocks` is one line:
+   - `cue`: the id the animation is keyed to. Keep the ten ids and their order:
+     `intro, measure, covid, proof, ai, others, japan, dollar, loop, gold`.
+   - `text`: the caption.
+   - `say`: what the voice model actually speaks (capitals and `!` push the delivery).
+   - `lead` / `tail` (optional): words spoken before/after the line to push the
+     delivery, then cut out. A line with a `lead` is also mastered louder: the
+     lines without one (`intro` .. `japan`) stay level and the rest rise to the end.
+   - `gapAfter`: seconds of silence after the line.
+
+   `clips[0].takes` groups cues into generations, each with a `seed`; change a
+   seed to get a different read of that take.
+2. Check it quickly (regenerates the voice, then one still per cue, no render):
+
+       ./build.sh --voice --stills
+
+   Look at `output/gromen-inflate-stills/` (repo root). `NN-<cue>.png` is 1.5 s
+   into each line; the last one is the final frame.
+3. Ship it (voice, full render, page, deploy). The deploy is private unless
+   `--public` or `--tunnel` is given:
+
+       ./build.sh --voice --publish
+       ./build.sh --publish --tunnel
+
+Drop `--voice` when only the visuals changed. `./build.sh --help` lists the
+options and the environment variables for the toolchain and paths.
+
+## Where things are
+
+- `src/main.rs`: the diagram and choreography. The diagram is four regions of
+  one world (yardstick, the four exits, Japan vs USA, the doom loop) and the
+  camera pans between them. Every beat is placed relative to a cue's start or
+  end in `narration/timeline.json`, never at an absolute time. The lower-left
+  beat labels are each line's `text`; `shortened` in `build` overrides one that
+  is too long for the frame.
+- `voice.py`: writes `narration/timeline.json` and `narration/continuous.m4a`.
+- `package.py`: turns `output/gromen-inflate-raw.mp4` into
+  `output/gromen-inflate-public/` (page, captions, poster, `source.zip`).
+
+Colour emoji and flag glyphs only render in the screen-space text (header and
+beat labels). Text inside the diagram is monochrome, so the Japan and US flags
+there are drawn from rectangles and circles.
+
+A calm take that runs much past 45 s loses a sentence (Orpheus stops or skips
+near its end), so keep `takes` groups shorter than that.
+
+`TIMELINE=/path/to/timeline.json ./build.sh --stills` checks the choreography
+against other timings without touching the narration.
